            "merged_at": "2026-10-17T11:53:54Z"
          },
          "body": "The Node fingerprint test fails on a dual-stack local listener when the peer address is `::ffff:127.0.0.1`. This is a valid loopback address, but the existing expectation accepts only `0.0.0.0` or `::1` (and does not anchor both alternatives).\n\nAccept the exact loopback forms `127.0.0.1` and `::ffff:127.0.0.1` alongside the existing values, with the entire expression anchored. Arbitrary addresses and partial string matches still fail. No runtime behavior changes.\n\nValidation on Node 24.21.0:\n- The unchanged assertion reproduced one failure in `test/utils.test.ts` (197 passed).\n- `pnpm test`: lint, formatting, typecheck and coverage passed; 3,036 tests passed, 51 skipped after `pnpm build` (matching the CI build/test order).\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Expanded coverage for valid request IP addresses on non-web targets.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
